cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "pinn-audit: a reproducible audit of when physics-informed neural networks beat classical PDE solvers"
abstract: >-
  A single-repository benchmark testing the claim that physics-informed neural
  networks are competitive with classical numerical methods. Forward and inverse
  problems for the heat, wave, Burgers and Poisson equations are scored against
  closed-form analytic solutions on accuracy, wall-clock cost, and robustness to
  sparse and noisy observations.
authors:
  - family-names: Hasan
    given-names: Ridoy
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
keywords:
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - scientific machine learning
  - partial differential equations
  - reproducibility
